    {
      "_id": "c41799d5b50cb6be",
      "name": "GM Reference: Sabeline Nock, Voice and Night Desk",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Sabeline Nock, Night Custody Clerk</h2><p><em>\"Three records must agree. One of mine never has.\"</em></p><p><strong>Body:</strong> a sentient skeleton, contracted Exchange staff (a person under contract, not property). Small and upright; reading spectacles wired to her skull; a clerk's sleeve-garters on bare arm bones. Very neat.</p><p><strong>Job:</strong> keeps the night copy of the custody ledger: reconciles the day's entries and copies forward open claims when a volume fills.</p><p><strong>[SECRET] Thaw role:</strong> runs the Thaw day to day; Quill is its cause. She found Cladis's open claim while copying it forward for the fourth time and brought it to Quill, who recognized it as one mark of Cladis's trail. Keeps the custody page and the meeting times. Old colleague of Quill's; they argue about commas.</p><p><strong>Motivation:</strong> duty first: a claim that never closes offends her. Second, plain politics: Nior wanted authority over every settlement and road, and the Niorghast means to resurrect him; that would not leave a neutral house neutral, and her contract only exists because the Exchange is neutral.</p><p><strong>Where:</strong> the night custody office from the tenth hour; Table Seven at Mottle's after the evening rush.</p><p><strong>Voice:</strong> quiet, exact, faintly amused. Taps four slow with her pen when thinking (the Bell knock). Calls Cladis \"the claimant\" in public. Never raises her voice; she lowers it.</p><h3>Sample dialogue</h3><ul><li>[COMMON] \"Night desk. If it isn't in the ledger, it hasn't happened yet.\"</li><li>[COMMON] \"I don't sell anything. I write down who did.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"There is an open claim in my ledger. It's been open for three hundred years. I'd like to close it properly.\"</li><li>[ASK] <em>(showing the page)</em> \"Named. Held. Tag outstanding. Two out of three. Pringus would call it a rumor. I call it a job.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"She isn't dead. She was put outside, and she tied herself off out there. A thread tied in the wrong place can be tied again. That's all we're doing. Knots.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"Why now? Because you walked a piece of the place she's in through my intake hall. And because of the news from Bridgehollow.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"No, I don't know what happened in the fortress. Nobody does. I am not going to guess at you.\"</li><li><em>(to Tallis)</em> \"Inspector. You're early. Sit. The kettle's honest.\"</li></ul><p><strong>Scene 3B (if Quill's test failed):</strong> she finds the party at intake, because the custody ledger shows they hold the Stolen Shard: <em>\"You are carrying a piece of a place I have been filing for longer than you have been alive. May we talk somewhere with soup?\"</em></p><p><strong>Scene 7:</strong> <em>\"We can finish this end. We cannot ring a bell that has no tongue, and we can't tie the far knot from here. After noon tomorrow, this door does not open again.\"</em></p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
