    {
      "_id": "538952205d96297d",
      "name": "Lore Reference: The Open Claim",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>The Open Claim</h2><p>[ASK] The custody line, copied forward for about three hundred years: <em>\"Cladis. Named. Held: the place where even time cannot leave. Tag: outstanding.\"</em> The same words are cut into the Stolen Shard.</p><p><strong>Why it is a \"rumor\":</strong> the Exchange accepts a named person into a body only when three records agree: the intake ledger (her name), the custody ledger (the \"held\" line) and the physical tag. Intake and custody agree; the tag has been outstanding for 300 years. Two out of three is a rumor (Pringus's rule).</p><p>[EARN] The claim is one mark of Cladis's trail, left on purpose (with the CLADIS marks on Europa's father's map and the old intake tag from the Session 12 passage).</p><p><strong>She knows:</strong> the open claim, the method, every Thaw member, the cold door's timetable, Tallis's interest. <strong>She does not know:</strong> who banished Cladis, what happened in Nior's fortress, who cut the sentence, or whether it will work. She knows <em>of</em> the Goddess's name but has never heard it said. [SECRET] She says \"I don't know\" about the fortress plainly.</p><p><strong>Secrecy:</strong> she never says \"Cladis\" in a common hall (\"the claimant\", \"her\"). The page is shown once, at Table Seven, or Pringus finds it during an audit.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
