    {
      "_id": "e82612a8f437d658",
      "name": "Side Quest: The Outstanding Tag",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Side Quest: The Outstanding Tag (Part 7, T5)</h2><p><strong>Hook:</strong> intake and custody agree; the physical tag has been \"outstanding\" for 300 years. Find it and make the three records agree.</p><h3>Objectives</h3><ul><li><strong>Find the tag.</strong> It is among the old intake tags from the Session 12 chest and passage material. If the party took them: Investigation <strong>DC 12</strong> to spot a tag stamped with the Winter crown's mark and an intake number matching Sabeline's page. If not: it is still in the passage under the Cladis memorial (History <strong>DC 12</strong> to read the old numbering).</li><li><strong>Second path:</strong> the Rite of the Remaining Bone (Expose Claim, 10 minutes, a copper coin, no charges) on the tag shows the claim it belongs to.</li><li><strong>Present it.</strong> A party member with custody presents the tag to Pringus for a Reconciliation Audit: <em>\"I know this tag is real. The ledger states the claim is open. I infer it was left to be found. I do not know what is at the other end.\"</em> Once all three agree, the claim is reconciled and the threshold will accept the named person.</li></ul><p><strong>Warning:</strong> an audit is a <em>public</em> record. Inspector Tallis reads audits. Doing it honestly makes the operation legal and visible; skipping it makes it invisible and impossible. A completed audit gives advantage when talking Tallis down (Scene 5).</p><p><strong>Reward:</strong> the records agree; Tallis can be talked down (delay DC 15, permit DC 17).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
